ong debate the main  focus was on her from the start she  dominated the first hour finished  strongly ended up with the most speaking  time but actually all four of the top  tier candidates including Bernie Sanders  Joe Biden and pipa de jedge had strong  debates and so did the second tier  candidates  Cory Booker Kamala Harris and and also  Amy Klobuchar  and the most important thing here was  that the message and tone overall was  this message of civility and unity it's  very clear that the Democrats are trying  to portray themselves as the adults in  the room in direct contrast to the  circus that is the Trump White House in  a time of social media in a time of  spin-doctors and spin and Twitter and  just to be clear politicians telling  lies on social media platforms how long  until the Democratic candidates the  Democrat candidates choose to or are  allowed to pitch themselves based on the  bread-and-butter issues you know how  much money you've got in the bank how  much tax you're paying whether your job  is secure the kind of things that people  really want to vote on I like I said you  know there were a lot of substantive  issues covered in this particular debate  there could still have been so much more  I mean we we we didn't discuss economic  inequality at all we didn't discuss  issues in the the public education  system we didn't discuss gun violence  and these are important issues that  Americans care about and they want to  hear more about these issues but we did  discuss very important issues including  what I appreciated was a focus on  climate change that was a very important  thing to focus on we had it we had a  good set of remarks on that and certain  candidates kept coming back to that we  also had some really interesting things  brought up for example about child care  and paid family leave the importance of  military and other types of service to  our country so there are a lot of issues  on the minds of Americans and in each of  these debates